You can use a Python geocoding package in Databricks (e.g., geopy with OpenStreetMap Nominatim) so you don’t need an API key, but there are two important caveats:

Nominatim’s usage policy forbids heavy/bulk geocoding; 100k addresses at ~1 request/second will take many hours and may violate their ToS.
There is no offline package that can reliably give street‑level lat/long for arbitrary US addresses without hitting some external service or internal geocoder.

So the code below is technically how to do it, but you should clear it with your IT/lead before running on all 100k. It’s safer to run on a smaller subset or use an approved, bulk geocoding service.

